1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,443
a free open-source RSS tool,

2
00:00:02,443 --> 00:00:05,520
enhanced with AI, makes this MrRSS

3
00:00:05,520 --> 00:00:08,300
subscribed foreign content can be smartly translated;

4
00:00:08,300 --> 00:00:10,348
complex info can be quickly summarized,

5
00:00:10,348 --> 00:00:12,039
and content with knowledge gaps

6
00:00:12,039 --> 00:00:14,770
can be discussed in chats for basic understanding

7
00:00:15,170 --> 00:00:19,410
This is a modern, cross-platform, free AI RSS reader app.

8
00:00:20,010 --> 00:00:22,190
There are three modes when adding feeds:

9
00:00:22,190 --> 00:00:24,260
regular users can just paste feed URLs,

10
00:00:24,260 --> 00:00:26,246
while advanced users can use scripts,

11
00:00:26,246 --> 00:00:28,730
parse web content, or use email subscriptions

12
00:00:29,210 --> 00:00:29,753
Once set up,

13
00:00:29,753 --> 00:00:32,770
each can have its own network settings and view modes chosen.

14
00:00:33,260 --> 00:00:33,265
images received should display fine, though some sites may block scrapers, causing images to fail loading.

15
00:00:39,230 --> 00:00:40,010
at this point,

16
00:00:40,010 --> 00:00:42,890
head to 'Settings' and enable 'Enable Media Cache',

17
00:00:42,890 --> 00:00:44,870
then restart the app to try again

18
00:00:45,350 --> 00:00:47,767
If you wish to tweak the reading view,

19
00:00:47,767 --> 00:00:49,728
you can customize CSS styles.

20
00:00:49,728 --> 00:00:52,276
Click the Help button to see the guide;

21
00:00:52,276 --> 00:00:54,759
if unsure, let the AI craft one for you.

22
00:00:55,040 --> 00:00:58,240
you can tweak font styles for content in the author's sample.

23
00:00:58,760 --> 00:01:01,378
if you dislike some of your subscribed content

24
00:01:01,378 --> 00:01:03,200
or have Special Follow keywords

25
00:01:03,690 --> 00:01:06,047
you can use its automation rules feature

26
00:01:06,047 --> 00:01:09,288
to perform various tagging actions on matching content,

27
00:01:09,288 --> 00:01:11,410
or use shortcuts for quick commands.

28
00:01:11,860 --> 00:01:13,251
For better AI results,

29
00:01:13,251 --> 00:01:16,300
you must enter the model Key and API endpoint.

30
00:01:16,780 --> 00:01:19,412
this URL might differ from the default one,

31
00:01:19,412 --> 00:01:21,105
which usually ends with /v1,

32
00:01:21,105 --> 00:01:22,547
but to connect smoothly,

33
00:01:22,547 --> 00:01:25,870
you need to use /v1/chat/completions — keep that in mind.

34
00:01:26,250 --> 00:01:28,650
then you can switch to AI summaries in Settings

35
00:01:29,010 --> 00:01:30,905
Here's how it works in practice:

36
00:01:30,905 --> 00:01:33,333
the AI chat is in the bottom-right corner,

37
00:01:33,333 --> 00:01:35,999
handy for reading professional foreign posts.

38
00:01:36,410 --> 00:01:39,137
Besides these, MrRSS has some neat features —

39
00:01:39,137 --> 00:01:42,689
one lets you discover new feeds right from existing ones.

40
00:01:43,010 --> 00:01:46,506
it can auto-enable waterfall layouts for image feeds,

41
00:01:46,506 --> 00:01:49,330
and integrates with Obsidian and FreshRSS

42
00:01:49,450 --> 00:01:51,173
you won't have to worry about

43
00:01:51,173 --> 00:01:53,610
media piling up—you can set cache limits

44
00:01:53,610 --> 00:01:54,740
and retention days.

45
00:01:55,020 --> 00:01:56,782
the overall look is clean and neat,

46
00:01:56,782 --> 00:01:58,700
making it pleasant for reading feeds.

47
00:01:59,280 --> 00:02:02,947
For image content, you can zoom in/out with your mouse;

48
00:02:02,947 --> 00:02:04,400
press Ctrl+S to save.

49
00:02:04,790 --> 00:02:05,936
If for long posts

50
00:02:05,936 --> 00:02:09,038
a full-screen immersive mode were added later,

51
00:02:09,038 --> 00:02:10,389
that would be ideal.

52
00:02:10,770 --> 00:02:11,763
With mouse gestures,

53
00:02:11,763 --> 00:02:14,170
most actions can be done without the keyboard.

54
00:02:14,570 --> 00:02:16,124
some bloggers may see RSS tools

55
00:02:16,124 --> 00:02:18,883
as ways to break through or trim an information cocoon,

56
00:02:18,883 --> 00:02:20,790
but they don't actually work that way

57
00:02:21,070 --> 00:02:22,970
if you wish to follow more content,

58
00:02:22,970 --> 00:02:25,990
you already have reading tastes and a hunger to learn.

59
00:02:26,540 --> 00:02:29,406
RSS tools can help you swiftly filter messages

60
00:02:29,406 --> 00:02:31,900
and mark which ones you've already read.

61
00:02:32,100 --> 00:02:34,818
From this perspective, MrRSS is a solid filter tool —

62
00:02:34,818 --> 00:02:36,683
you can find content you care about

63
00:02:36,683 --> 00:02:38,709
from sites that support subscriptions.

64
00:02:38,950 --> 00:02:40,730
come back after some time to reap,

65
00:02:40,730 --> 00:02:42,350
be a data hive of the new age

